ed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},"acme-oauth2":{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Acme OAuth",visibility:"staff",vertical:["social-media"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-acme-oauth2.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Acme OAuth to obtain and refresh access tokens via OAuth2.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Acme OAuth connector via the proxy pattern to interact with the API. Common endpoints include: GET /token (fetch access token), POST /token/refresh (refresh token), GET /userinfo (fetch user info), POST /revoke (revoke token). Remember that requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic auth injection—use connectors.proxy("acme‑oauth2", "/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},agentmail:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"AgentMail",visibility:"ga",vertical:["communication"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-agentmail.svg",authType:"API_KEY",description:"Connect to AgentMail to programmatically create and manage AI agent email inboxes.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the AgentMail connector via the proxy pattern to manage inboxes, messages, threads, API keys, and webhooks. Common endpoints include: POST /v0/inboxes (create inbox), GET /v0/inboxes/{inboxId}/messages (list messages), POST /v0/inboxes/{inboxId}/messages (send message), GET /v0/api-keys (list API keys), and POST /v0/webhooks (register webhook). Requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic auth injection. Prefer using: connectors.proxy("agentmail", "/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},amplitude:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Amplitude",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["other"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-amplitude.svg",authType:"API_KEY",description:"Connect to Amplitude to ingest events and interact with analytics and export APIs.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Amplitude connector via the proxy pattern, e.g. connectors.proxy("amplitude", "/httpapi") for sending events (HTTP API V2 POST /httpapi); use connectors.proxy("amplitude", "/export") to retrieve historical event data (GET /export); use connectors.proxy("amplitude", "/taxonomy") to manage event taxonomy (Taxonomy API operations such as DELETE and RESTORE). Requests are auto-authenticated via headers in the SDK proxy. Prefer using: connectors.proxy("amplitude", "/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},apollo:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!0,metadata:{verticals:["sales-engagement"],displayName:"Apollo",stage:"beta",logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-apollo.svg"}},asana:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Asana",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["ticketing"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-asana.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Asana to manage tasks, projects, workspaces, and team workflows.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Asana connector via the proxy pattern for authenticated API requests. Common endpoints: GET /api/1.0/workspaces to list workspaces, GET /api/1.0/projects to list projects, GET /api/1.0/tasks?project={project_gid} to list tasks in a project, GET /api/1.0/users/me to get the current user. All requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth token injection. Prefer using: connectors.proxy("asana", "/api/1.0/tasks?project={project_gid}"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{javascript:[{package_name:"asana",package_version:"3.0.12"}]}},links:{webUrl:"https://app.asana.com",apiDocsUrl:"https://developers.asana.com/docs"},integrationKeys:{nango:"asana"}}},ashby:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Ashby",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["ats"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-ashby.svg",authType:"API_KEY",description:"Connect to Ashby to access ATS data such as jobs, candidates, and applications.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use connectors.proxy("ashby", "/path") to interact with Ashby endpoints. Common endpoints include: POST /application.list, GET /job.info, GET /jobPosting.list, POST /candidate.create, and GET /jobBoard.list. Requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic auth injection. Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},bigquery:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Google BigQuery",visibility:"ga",vertical:["developer-tools"],audience:["enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-bigquery.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Google BigQuery to execute SQL queries on large datasets.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the @google-cloud/bigquery SDK through the proxy for authenticated BigQuery requests. The code_snippet in packages.javascript shows the full setup: stub GoogleAuth so the SDK never hits the GCP metadata server, point the BigQuery client at proxyUrl with customEndpoint: true, and use an interceptor that rewrites paths and injects proxy headers via connectors.getProxyHeaders("bigquery"). With this setup you can use the native SDK normally: bigquery.getDatasets(), bigquery.query({ query }), bigquery.dataset(id).getTables(), bigquery.dataset(id).table(id).getMetadata(), etc. The proxy resolves the real project ID and OAuth credentials automatically — never specify them in client code.',packages:{javascript:[{package_name:"@google-cloud/bigquery",package_version:"7.9.4",code_snippet:'import { BigQuery } from "@google-cloud/bigquery";\nimport { GoogleAuth, OAuth2Client } from "google-auth-library";\n\n// Stub auth so the SDK never uses ADC or the GCP metadata server.\nconst oauth = new OAuth2Client();\noauth.setCredentials({ access_token: "proxy-handled", expiry_date: Date.now() + 86400000 * 365 * 10 });\nconst auth = new GoogleAuth({ authClient: oauth });\nauth.getProjectId = async () => "_";\nauth.getClient = async () => oauth;\n\nconst bigquery = new BigQuery({ projectId: "_", customEndpoint: true, apiEndpoint: proxyUrl, authClient: auth });\n\n// Rewrite paths and inject proxy identity headers on every request.\nbigquery.interceptors.push({\n  async request(reqOpts) {\n    let path = reqOpts.uri.replace(/.*\\/projects\\/[^/]+/, "");\n    if (!path.startsWith("/")) path = "/" + path;\n    reqOpts.uri = proxyUrl + path;\n    const proxyHeaders = await connectors.getProxyHeaders("bigquery");\n    reqOpts.headers = { ...(reqOpts.headers ?? {}), ...proxyHeaders };\n    return reqOpts;\n  },\n});'},{package_name:"google-auth-library",package_version:"9.15.1"}]}},links:{webUrl:"https://cloud.google.com/bigquery",apiDocsUrl:"https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/rest"}}},bitbucket:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Bitbucket",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["developer-tools"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-bitbucket.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Bitbucket to manage repositories, pull requests, projects, and workspaces.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Bitbucket connector via the proxy pattern for authenticated API requests. Common endpoints: GET /2.0/repositories/{workspace}/{repo_slug} to get a repository, GET /2.0/repositories/{workspace}/{repo_slug}/pullrequests to list pull requests, GET /2.0/workspaces to list workspaces, GET /2.0/user/repositories to list authenticated user repositories. All requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth token injection. Prefer using: connectors.proxy("bitbucket", "/2.0/repositories/{workspace}/{repo_slug}"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{javascript:[{package_name:"bitbucket",package_version:"2.2.4"}]}},links:{webUrl:"https://bitbucket.org",apiDocsUrl:"https://developer.atlassian.com/cloud/bitbucket/rest/intro/"},integrationKeys:{nango:"bitbucket"}}},"bitbucket-source-control":{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Bitbucket",visibility:"beta",vertical:["developer-tools"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-bitbucket-source-control.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Bitbucket to access and manage repositories, pull requests, commits, and code search.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:"",packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},box:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Box",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["wiki","file-storage"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-box.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Box to manage files, folders, users, and webhooks via OAuth2 API.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Box connector via the proxy pattern to call common endpoints: GET /folders/:id to retrieve folder metadata, POST /files/content to upload files, GET /files/:id/content to download file content, and GET /webhooks to list webhook configurations. Requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic auth injection — call connectors.proxy("box", "/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""},integrationKeys:{nango:"box"}}},brave:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Brave",visibility:"beta",vertical:["other"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-brave.svg",authType:"API_KEY",description:"Connect to Brave to perform web, image, video, and LLM‑powered search queries.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Brave connector via the proxy pattern to access endpoints such as GET /res/v1/web/search, GET /res/v1/images/search, POST /res/v1/chat/completions, and GET /res/v1/summarizer/summary. Calls are proxied through the SDK, which automatically injects authentication headers. Prefer using: connectors.proxy("brave", "/res/v1/web/search") or similar paths for other endpoints. Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},calendly:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Calendly",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["other"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-calendly.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Calendly to manage scheduled events, event types, and invitees.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Calendly connector via the proxy pattern for authenticated API requests. Common endpoints: GET /v2/users/me to get the current user, GET /v2/event_types?user={user_uri} to list event types, GET /v2/scheduled_events to list scheduled events, GET /v2/scheduled_events/{uuid}/invitees to list invitees for an event. All requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth token injection. Prefer using: connectors.proxy("calendly", "/v2/scheduled_events"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{javascript:[{package_name:"calendly-js",package_version:"1.0.1"}]}},links:{webUrl:"https://calendly.com",apiDocsUrl:"https://developer.calendly.com/api-docs"},integrationKeys:{nango:"calendly"}}},clickup:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"ClickUp",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["ticketing"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-clickup.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to ClickUp to manage tasks, folders, lists, spaces, and workspaces.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the ClickUp connector via the proxy pattern for authenticated API requests. Common endpoints: GET /api/v2/team to list workspaces, GET /api/v2/team/{team_id}/space to list spaces, GET /api/v2/space/{space_id}/list to list lists, GET /api/v2/list/{list_id}/task to list tasks in a list, POST /api/v2/list/{list_id}/task to create a task. All requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth token injection. Prefer using: connectors.proxy("clickup", "/api/v2/team"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{javascript:[{package_name:"clickup.js",package_version:"2.2.0"}]}},links:{webUrl:"https://app.clickup.com",apiDocsUrl:"https://developer.clickup.com/reference"},integrationKeys:{nango:"clickup"}}},confluence:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Confluence",visibility:"ga",vertical:["wiki"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-confluence.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Confluence to interact with pages, spaces, content, and search via REST API.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'To use the Confluence connector via the proxy pattern, first retrieve your Atlassian cloud ID by calling GET /oauth/token/accessible-resources (returns an array of {id, url, name}). Then use cloud-scoped paths that include the /ex/confluence/{cloudId}/wiki prefix: GET /ex/confluence/{cloudId}/wiki/api/v2/pages (list pages), GET /ex/confluence/{cloudId}/wiki/api/v2/spaces (list spaces), POST /ex/confluence/{cloudId}/wiki/api/v2/pages (create page), GET /ex/confluence/{cloudId}/wiki/rest/api/content/{id} (retrieve content v1). Example: connectors.proxy("confluence", "/ex/confluence/{cloudId}/wiki/api/v2/pages"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""},integrationKeys:{nango:"confluence"}}},"custom-mcp":{hasClient:!0,hasServer:!0,metadata:{verticals:["other"],displayName:"Custom MCP",logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-custom-mcp.svg",stage:"beta",authType:"CUSTOM",connect_ui:{pre_connect_input:"custom",flow:"client_managed"}}},databricks:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Databricks for Databricks Apps (U2M)",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["developer-tools"],audience:["enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-databricks.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",connectionCheckFrequency:604800,description:"Connect to Databricks to execute queries and manage data. Used for Databricks Apps only via User-to-Machine (U2M) flow.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'## Mode 1 — SDK Proxy (REST API)\nThis mode is recommended for most use cases. It allows you to use the Databricks connector via the proxy pattern for authenticated REST API requests.\nThe proxy handles OAuth credentials and routing automatically — no SDK needed.\nStep 1 — Discover the warehouse ID:\n  GET /api/2.0/sql/warehouses/ → pick the warehouse_id from the response.\nStep 2 — Execute SQL via the Statement Execution API:\n  POST /api/2.0/sql/statements/ with body { "warehouse_id": "<id>", "statement": "<SQL>", "wait_timeout": "50s", "on_wait_timeout": "CONTINUE" }.\n  If status.state is "SUCCEEDED", rows are in result.data_array and column metadata in manifest.schema.columns.\n  If status.state is "PENDING" or "RUNNING", poll GET /api/2.0/sql/statements/{statement_id} until it completes.\nCommon SQL queries: SHOW CATALOGS, SHOW DATABASES, SHOW SCHEMAS, SHOW TABLES IN schema_name,\nDESCRIBE TABLE schema_name.table_name, SELECT * FROM schema_name.table_name LIMIT 10.\n\n## Mode 2 — Databricks CLI\nFor CLI operations (apps deploy, genie, workspace exploration), use the CLI proxy wrapper.\nThe token embeds your Replit identity and connection ID. The server validates\nyour identity, injects real Databricks credentials, and proxies the request.\nSecrets never leave the server. The token contains a space so it must be passed\nvia subprocess env (not shell export) to avoid shell parsing issues.\n\n```ts\nimport { ReplitConnectors } from "@replit/connectors-sdk";\nimport { execSync } from "child_process";\n\nconst connectors = new ReplitConnectors();\nconst config = await connectors.getCliConfig("databricks");\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst result = execSync(`databricks ${args.join(" ")}`, {\n  encoding: "utf-8",\n  env: {\n    ...process.env,\n    DATABRICKS_HOST: config.host,\n    DATABRICKS_TOKEN: config.token,\n  },\n});\n```\n\nWhen to use each mode:\n  - SDK Proxy: SQL queries, programmatic API calls from code\n  - CLI Proxy: databricks apps deploy, databricks apps init, databricks genie, workspace exploration with CLI',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"https://www.databricks.com",apiDocsUrl:"https://docs.databricks.com/dev-tools/api/latest/"}}},"databricks-m2m":{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!0,metadata:{verticals:["developer-tools"],audience:["enterprise"],displayName:"Databricks (Service Principal)",visibility:"alpha",logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-databricks.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Databricks to execute queries and manage data using a Service Principal.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'## Mode 1 — SDK Proxy (REST API)\nThis mode is recommended for most use cases. It allows you to use the Databricks connector via the proxy pattern for authenticated REST API requests.\nThe proxy handles OAuth credentials and routing automatically — no SDK needed.\nStep 1 — Discover the warehouse ID:\n  GET /api/2.0/sql/warehouses/ → pick the warehouse_id from the response.\nStep 2 — Execute SQL via the Statement Execution API:\n  POST /api/2.0/sql/statements/ with body { "warehouse_id": "<id>", "statement": "<SQL>", "wait_timeout": "50s", "on_wait_timeout": "CONTINUE" }.\n  If status.state is "SUCCEEDED", rows are in result.data_array and column metadata in manifest.schema.columns.\n  If status.state is "PENDING" or "RUNNING", poll GET /api/2.0/sql/statements/{statement_id} until it completes.\nCommon SQL queries: SHOW CATALOGS, SHOW DATABASES, SHOW SCHEMAS, SHOW TABLES IN schema_name,\nDESCRIBE TABLE schema_name.table_name, SELECT * FROM schema_name.table_name LIMIT 10.\n\n## Mode 2 — Databricks CLI\nFor CLI operations (apps deploy, genie, workspace exploration), use the CLI proxy wrapper.\nThe token embeds your Replit identity and connection ID. The server validates\nyour identity, injects real Databricks credentials, and proxies the request.\nSecrets never leave the server. The token contains a space so it must be passed\nvia subprocess env (not shell export) to avoid shell parsing issues.\n\n```ts\nimport { ReplitConnectors } from "@replit/connectors-sdk";\nimport { execSync } from "child_process";\n\nconst connectors = new ReplitConnectors();\nconst config = await connectors.getCliConfig("databricks-m2m");\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst result = execSync(`databricks ${args.join(" ")}`, {\n  encoding: "utf-8",\n  env: {\n    ...process.env,\n    DATABRICKS_HOST: config.host,\n    DATABRICKS_TOKEN: config.token,\n  },\n});\n```\n\nWhen to use each mode:\n  - SDK Proxy: SQL queries, programmatic API calls from code\n  - CLI Proxy: databricks apps deploy, databricks apps init, databricks genie, workspace exploration with CLI',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"https://www.databricks.com",apiDocsUrl:"https://docs.databricks.com/dev-tools/api/latest/"}}},discord:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Discord",visibility:"ga",vertical:["social-media"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-discord.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Discord to access user info, channels, messages, and OAuth2 flows.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Discord connector via the proxy pattern to call common endpoints—e.g., GET /users/@me to retrieve authenticated user info, GET /channels/{channel.id}/messages to list channel messages, POST /channels/{channel.id}/messages to create messages, GET /channels/{channel.id}/invites to list invites. Requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic auth injection; use connectors.proxy("discord", "/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""},integrationKeys:{nango:"discord"}}},dropbox:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Dropbox",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["wiki","file-storage"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-dropbox.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Dropbox to manage files, metadata, uploads, downloads, and account info.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Dropbox connector via the proxy pattern by calling connectors.proxy("dropbox", "/path"). Common endpoints include: POST /2/users/get_current_account, POST /2/files/list_folder, POST /2/files/upload, POST /2/files/download, and POST /2/files/get_metadata. Requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth2 token injection and refresh. Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""},integrationKeys:{nango:"dropbox"}}},elevenlabs:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"ElevenLabs",visibility:"beta",vertical:["communication","other"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-elevenlabs.svg",authType:"API_KEY",description:"Connect to ElevenLabs to convert text to speech, transcribe audio, and manage voices.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use this connector to interact with ElevenLabs’ API via the proxy pattern. Commonly used endpoints include: GET /v1/models, GET /v1/voices, POST /v1/text-to-speech/{voice_id}, and GET /v1/languages. Requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic authentication injected into headers. To send a request, use connectors.proxy("elevenlabs", "/v1/text-to-speech/{voice_id}") or similar. Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},figma:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Figma",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["other"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-figma.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Figma to access and interact with design files, comments, users, projects, and more.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Figma connector via the proxy pattern to access common endpoints like GET /v1/me (fetch authenticated user), GET /v1/files/:file_key (retrieve file data), GET /v1/projects/:project_id/files (list files in a project), GET /v1/files/:file_key/versions (retrieve file versions), and GET /v1/images/:file_key (generate images). Requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth2 token injection and refresh. Use connectors.proxy("figma", "/path") to call the API. Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""},integrationKeys:{nango:"figma"}}},firecrawl:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Firecrawl",visibility:"beta",vertical:["enrichment"],audience:["paid"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-firecrawl.svg",authType:"API_KEY",blueprint:{agentInstructions:"",packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},github:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"GitHub",visibility:"ga",vertical:["developer-tools","ticketing"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-github.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",connectionCheckFrequency:82800,description:"Connect to GitHub to manage repositories, issues, pull requests, and more.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the GitHub connector via the proxy pattern for authenticated API requests. Common endpoints: GET /repos/{owner}/{repo} to get a repository, GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues to list issues, GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls to list pull requests, GET /user/repos to list authenticated user repositories. All requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth token injection. Prefer using: connectors.proxy("github", "/repos/{owner}/{repo}"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{javascript:[{package_name:"@octokit/rest",package_version:"21.1.1"}]}},links:{webUrl:"https://github.com",apiDocsUrl:"https://docs.github.com/en/rest"},integrationKeys:{nango:"github"}}},"github-source-control":{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"GitHub",visibility:"beta",vertical:["developer-tools"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-github-source-control.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",connectionCheckFrequency:82800,description:"Connect to GitHub to access repositories, issues, pull requests, and authorizations.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:"",packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},"gitlab-source-control":{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"GitLab",visibility:"beta",vertical:["developer-tools","ticketing"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-gitlab-source-control.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to GitLab to access projects, repositories, issues, and user data via OAuth2.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:"",packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},"google-calendar":{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Google Calendar",visibility:"ga",vertical:["other"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-google-calendar.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Google Calendar to retrieve, create, update, and manage calendars and events.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Google Calendar connector via the proxy pattern by calling connectors.proxy("google-calendar", "/path")—requests are automatically authenticated with OAuth2 tokens injected and refreshed by the SDK. Commonly useful API endpoints include: GET /calendars/{calendarId}/events, POST /calendars/{calendarId}/events, PATCH /calendars/{calendarId}/events/{eventId}, GET /users/me/calendarList, POST /calendars/{calendarId}/acl. Note that the proxy returns a raw response object—use .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""},integrationKeys:{nango:"google-calendar"}}},"google-docs":{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Google Docs",visibility:"ga",vertical:["other"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-google-docs.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Google Docs to create, read, and update documents.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'To use the Google Docs connector, call common REST endpoints such as POST /v1/documents (create a blank document), GET /v1/documents/{documentId} (retrieve a document), and POST /v1/documents/{documentId}:batchUpdate (apply updates). You can also use POST /v1/documents/{documentId}:batchUpdate for rich editing operations. All requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth2 token injection and refreshing — simply use connectors.proxy("google-docs", "/v1/documents/{path}"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""},integrationKeys:{nango:"google-docs"}}},"google-drive":{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Google Drive",visibility:"ga",vertical:["wiki","file-storage"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-google-drive.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Google Drive to manage files and documents.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Google Drive connector via the proxy pattern for authenticated API requests. Common endpoints: GET /drive/v3/files to list files, GET /drive/v3/files/{fileId} to get file metadata, POST /upload/drive/v3/files to upload files. All requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth token injection and refresh. Prefer using: connectors.proxy("google-drive", "/drive/v3/files"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{javascript:[{package_name:"googleapis",package_version:"148.0.0"}]}},links:{webUrl:"https://drive.google.com",apiDocsUrl:"https://developers.google.com/drive"},integrationKeys:{nango:"google-drive"}}},"google-mail":{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Gmail",visibility:"ga",vertical:["other"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-google-mail.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Gmail to manage messages, drafts, labels, threads, and more via API.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Gmail connector via the proxy pattern: you can call endpoints like GET /gmail/v1/users/me/messages (list messages), GET /gmail/v1/users/me/messages/{messageId} (get a message), POST /gmail/v1/users/me/messages/send (send a message), GET /gmail/v1/users/me/labels (list labels), POST /gmail/v1/users/me/drafts (create a draft). Requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth2 token injection and refresh. Prefer using: connectors.proxy("google-mail","/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""},integrationKeys:{nango:"google-mail"}}},"google-sheet":{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Google Sheets",visibility:"ga",vertical:["other"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-google-sheet.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Google Sheets to read, write, and modify spreadsheet data via REST API.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'To use the Google Sheets connector via the proxy pattern, you can call common endpoints like: POST /v4/spreadsheets (create spreadsheet), GET /v4/spreadsheets/{spreadsheetId} (get spreadsheet), POST /v4/spreadsheets/{spreadsheetId}:batchUpdate (apply updates), POST /v4/spreadsheets/{spreadsheetId}/values/{range}:append (append values), GET /v4/spreadsheets/{spreadsheetId}/values:batchGet (retrieve multiple ranges). Use connectors.proxy("google-sheet", "/v4/spreadsheets/{spreadsheetId}/values/{range}:append") to make requests — authentication and token refresh are handled automatically. Prefer using connectors.proxy("google-sheet", "/path") for all calls. Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""},integrationKeys:{nango:"google-sheet"}}},"google-slides":{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Google Slides",visibility:"ga",vertical:["other"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-google-slides.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Google Slides to create and manage presentations.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Google Slides connector via the proxy pattern for authenticated API requests. Under the hood this connector uses Google Drive OAuth, so all requests go through the Drive API. Common endpoints: GET /drive/v3/files?q=mimeType%3D%27application/vnd.google-apps.presentation%27 to list presentations, GET /drive/v3/files/{fileId} to get presentation metadata, GET /drive/v3/files/{fileId}/export?mimeType=application/pdf to export a presentation. All requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth token injection and refresh. Prefer using: connectors.proxy("google-slides", "/drive/v3/files?q=mimeType%3D%27application/vnd.google-apps.presentation%27"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{javascript:[{package_name:"googleapis",package_version:"148.0.0"}]}},links:{webUrl:"https://slides.google.com",apiDocsUrl:"https://developers.google.com/slides"},integrationKeys:{nango:"google-slides"}}},hex:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Hex",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["other"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-hex.svg",authType:"API_KEY",description:"Connect to Hex to programmatically list, run, and manage projects in your Hex workspace.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Hex connector via the proxy pattern by calling connectors.proxy("hex", "/path"). Common endpoints include: GET /projects (list projects), POST /projects/{project_id}/runs (trigger a run), GET /projects/{project_id}/runs (list or check status), PATCH /data‑connections/{id} (rotate data connection credentials), and DELETE /projects/{project_id}/runs/{run_id} (cancel a run). Requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic API‑key‑based authentication injected in headers. Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},hubspot:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"HubSpot",visibility:"ga",vertical:["ticketing","crm"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-hubspot.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to HubSpot to manage contacts, companies, deals, tickets, and marketing campaigns.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the HubSpot connector via the proxy pattern for authenticated API requests. Common endpoints: GET /crm/v3/objects/contacts to list contacts, GET /crm/v3/objects/companies to list companies, GET /crm/v3/objects/deals to list deals, GET /crm/v3/objects/tickets to list tickets. All requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth token injection. Prefer using: connectors.proxy("hubspot", "/crm/v3/objects/contacts"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{javascript:[{package_name:"@hubspot/api-client",package_version:"12.0.0"}]}},links:{webUrl:"https://www.hubspot.com",apiDocsUrl:"https://developers.hubspot.com/docs/api/overview"}}},instagram:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Instagram",visibility:"ga",vertical:["social-media"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-instagram.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Instagram to access business/creator account media, profile, publish, and insights via OAuth2.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Instagram connector via the proxy pattern for common tasks. Typical useful endpoints include: GET /me?fields=id,username,account_type (to fetch account info); GET /{ig-user-id}/media?fields=id,caption,media_url,permalink (to list media); POST /{ig-user-id}/media (to create a media container); POST /{ig-user-id}/media_publish (to publish media); GET /{ig-user-id}/insights?metric=impressions,reach (to fetch insights). Requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic auth injection — use connectors.proxy("instagram", "/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},jira:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Jira",visibility:"ga",vertical:["ticketing"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-jira.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Jira to perform issue, project, webhook, and board operations via REST APIs.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'To use the Jira connector via the proxy pattern, first retrieve your Atlassian cloud ID by calling GET /oauth/token/accessible-resources (returns an array of {id, url, name}). Then use cloud-scoped paths that include the /ex/jira/{cloudId} prefix: GET /ex/jira/{cloudId}/rest/api/3/issue/{issueIdOrKey}, POST /ex/jira/{cloudId}/rest/api/3/issue, GET /ex/jira/{cloudId}/rest/api/3/project, POST /ex/jira/{cloudId}/rest/api/3/webhook. Example: connectors.proxy("jira", "/ex/jira/{cloudId}/rest/api/3/issue/TEST-1"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},linear:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Linear",visibility:"ga",vertical:["ticketing"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-linear.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",connectionCheckFrequency:2592e3,description:"Connect to Linear to query issues, projects, cycles, and manage issue tracking via GraphQL.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Linear connector via the proxy pattern to interact with Linear’s GraphQL API. Common API operations include: (1) GET authenticated user details (query viewer { id name email }), (2) GET list of issues (query issues { nodes { id title } }), (3) CREATE an issue (mutation issueCreate), (4) UPDATE an issue (mutation issueUpdate), and (5) LIST projects (query projects { nodes { id name } }). All requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth2 token injection—use connectors.proxy("linear", "/graphql", { query: "..." }). Prefer using: connectors.proxy("linear", "/graphql"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},"microsoft-fabric":{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Microsoft Fabric",visibility:"beta",vertical:["developer-tools"],audience:["enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-microsoft-fabric.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Microsoft Fabric to access data engineering, data science, and analytics workloads.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Microsoft Fabric connector via the proxy pattern for authenticated REST API requests. The proxy handles OAuth credentials and routing automatically — no SDK needed.\nCommon endpoints:\n  GET /v1/workspaces — List all workspaces the user has access to.\n  GET /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/items — List items in a workspace.\n  GET /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/lakehouses — List lakehouses in a workspace.\n  GET /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/warehouses — List warehouses in a workspace.\n  POST /v1/workspaces/{workspaceId}/items/{itemId}/jobs/instances?jobType=RunNotebook — Run a notebook.\nPrefer using: connectors.proxy("microsoft-fabric", "/v1/workspaces", { method: "GET" }). The response is a raw Response object, so you need to parse it using the Response.json() method.',packages:{javascript:[{package_name:"node-fetch",package_version:"3.3.2",code_snippet:'const response = await connectors.proxy("microsoft-fabric", "/v1/workspaces", { method: "GET" });\nconst data = await response.json();\nconsole.log(data);'}]}},links:{webUrl:"https://app.fabric.microsoft.com",apiDocsUrl:"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/fabric/articles/"}}},monday:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Monday",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["ticketing"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-monday.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Monday to query and manipulate boards, items, users, and more via GraphQL API.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Monday connector via the proxy pattern to interact with the Monday.com GraphQL API. Common endpoints include: POST /v2 to run queries (e.g., fetch boards), POST /v2 to create items, and POST /v2 to update column values. Always send GraphQL queries or mutations as POST to /v2, including query and optional variables in the JSON body. Use connectors.proxy("monday", "/v2") — requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth token injection. Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""},integrationKeys:{nango:"monday"}}},"nano-banana":{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Nano Banana",visibility:"beta",vertical:["other"],audience:["paid"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-nano-banana.svg",authType:"API_KEY",blueprint:{agentInstructions:"",packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},notion:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Notion",visibility:"ga",vertical:["wiki"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-notion.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Notion to manage pages, databases, and workspace content.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Notion connector via the proxy pattern for authenticated API requests. The Notion-Version header is injected automatically by the proxy — never set it manually. Common endpoints: GET /v1/users/me to get the current user, POST /v1/search to search pages and databases, POST /v1/databases/{database_id}/query to query a database, GET /v1/pages/{page_id} to get a page, POST /v1/pages to create a page. Prefer using: connectors.proxy("notion", "/v1/search"). The proxy returns a raw response object — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{javascript:[{package_name:"@notionhq/client",package_version:"2.3.0"}]}},links:{webUrl:"https://notion.so",apiDocsUrl:"https://developers.notion.com/reference/intro"},integrationKeys:{nango:"notion"}}},onedrive:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Microsoft OneDrive",visibility:"ga",vertical:["other"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-onedrive.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Microsoft OneDrive to manage and interact with files via Microsoft Graph.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Microsoft OneDrive connector via the proxy pattern to perform common operations such as: GET /me/drive/root/children to list files, GET /me/drive/items/{item-id} to get an item, POST /me/drive/items/{parent-id}/children to upload or create, PATCH /me/drive/items/{item-id} to update properties, and GET /me/drive/root/delta to track changes. Make calls via connectors.proxy("onedrive", "/path") so that OAuth2 authorization is injected and refreshed automatically. Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""},integrationKeys:{nango:"onedrive"}}},openai:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"OpenAI",visibility:"beta",vertical:["other"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-openai.svg",authType:"API_KEY",description:"Connect to OpenAI to access models for chat, completions, edits, images, moderation, and more.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'To use the OpenAI connector via the proxy pattern, your agent can call common endpoints such as POST /chat/completions, POST /completions, GET /models, and POST /moderations. Requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic authentication headers. Use: connectors.proxy("openai", "/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},outlook:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Microsoft Outlook",visibility:"ga",vertical:["other"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-outlook.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Microsoft Outlook to access mail, calendar, contacts, and more via Microsoft Graph.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Microsoft Outlook connector via the proxy pattern by calling connectors.proxy("outlook", "/path"). Common useful API endpoints include GET /v1.0/me/messages (list emails), POST /v1.0/me/messages (create or send messages), GET /v1.0/me/events (list calendar events), POST /v1.0/me/events (create an event), and GET /v1.0/me/contacts (retrieve contacts). All requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth2 token injection and refresh. Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""},integrationKeys:{nango:"outlook"}}},plaid:{hasClient:!0,hasServer:!0,metadata:{verticals:["banking"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],displayName:"Plaid",stage:"ga",description:"Connect to Plaid to access financial data, bank accounts, and transactions.",logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-plaid.svg",links:{webUrl:"https://plaid.com",apiDocsUrl:"https://plaid.com/docs/"},blueprint:{agentInstructions:"Use the @replit/connectors-sdk with the official Plaid SDK to interact with the Plaid API via a secure proxy.\n\nThe getPlaidClient() function returns a fully configured Plaid client that:\n- Uses @replit/connectors-sdk for authentication and proxy routing\n- Works exactly like the official Plaid SDK\n- All credentials are managed securely by the proxy\n\nExample: Get account balances\n\n  const client = await getPlaidClient();\n\n  // Get all linked accounts\n  const accountsResponse = await client.accountsGet({});\n  console.log('Accounts:', accountsResponse.data.accounts);\n\n  // Get account balances\n  const balanceResponse = await client.accountsBalanceGet({});\n  for (const account of balanceResponse.data.accounts) {\n    console.log(account.name + ': $' + account.balances.current);\n  }\n\nExample: Get recent transactions\n\n  const client = await getPlaidClient();\n\n  const response = await client.transactionsGet({\n    start_date: '2024-01-01',\n    end_date: '2024-12-31',\n  });\n\n  for (const txn of response.data.transactions) {\n    console.log(txn.date + ' - ' + txn.name + ': $' + txn.amount);\n  }\n\nSee https://plaid.com/docs/api/ for all available methods.",packages:{javascript:[{package_name:"plaid",package_version:"40.0.0",code_snippet:"import { Configuration, PlaidApi, type PlaidApiInterface } from 'plaid';\n\n// Creates a Plaid client that uses the OpenInt proxy.\n// Auth headers are resolved fresh on every call so tokens never go stale in long-lived processes.\n// All API calls are automatically authenticated - credentials and access_token are injected by the proxy.\n//\n// Usage:\n//   const client = await getPlaidClient();\n//   const accounts = await client.accountsGet({});  // No access_token needed!\n//   const transactions = await client.transactionsGet({ start_date: '2024-01-01', end_date: '2024-12-31' });\n//\nexport async function getPlaidClient(): Promise<PlaidApiInterface> {\n  const proxyHeaders = await getProxyHeaders();\n\n  const configuration = new Configuration({\n    basePath: proxyUrl,\n    baseOptions: {\n      headers: proxyHeaders,\n    },\n  });\n\n  const rawClient = new PlaidApi(configuration);\n\n  // Wrap the client to allow omitting access_token (proxy injects it)\n  return new Proxy(rawClient, {\n    get(target, prop) {\n      const value = (target as any)[prop];\n      if (typeof value === 'function') {\n        return async (request: any = {}, ...args: any[]) => {\n          const patchedRequest = { access_token: '', ...request };\n          return value.call(target, patchedRequest, ...args);\n        };\n      }\n      return value;\n    }\n  }) as PlaidApiInterface;\n}"}]}}}},postgres:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!0,metadata:{verticals:["database"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-postgres.svg",stage:"ga"}},resend:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!0,metadata:{verticals:["other"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-resend.svg",stage:"ga",authType:"API_KEY"}},revenuecat:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"RevenueCat",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["commerce"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-revenuecat.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to RevenueCat to manage subscription products, entitlements, and metrics.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the RevenueCat connector via the proxy pattern (OAuth tokens are injected and refreshed automatically). Common API endpoints include: GET /v1/subscribers/{app_user_id}, GET /v2/projects/{projectId}/customers/{customerId}/subscriptions, POST /v2/projects/{projectId}/apps (app creation), GET /v2/projects/{projectId}/customers (list customers), and GET /metrics or Charts API endpoints for analytics. Requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic auth injection; use connectors.proxy("revenuecat", "/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},salesforce:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Salesforce",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["crm"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-salesforce.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",connectionCheckFrequency:86400,description:"Connect to Salesforce to access CRM data and platform services via REST endpoints.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Salesforce connector via the proxy pattern to send requests through the SDK with automatic OAuth token injection. Common API endpoints include:\n- GET /services/data/v{version}/sobjects/\n- POST /services/data/v{version}/query/\n- GET /services/data/v{version}/limits\nRequests should be routed using connectors.proxy("salesforce", "/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""},integrationKeys:{nango:"salesforce"}}},segment:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Segment",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["other"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-segment.svg",authType:"API_KEY",description:"Connect to Segment to manage workspaces, sources, destinations, warehouses, and tracking plans.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'To use the Segment connector via proxy, common endpoints include: GET /workspaces, GET /sources, GET /destinations, PATCH /sources/{sourceId}/settings, and GET /tracking-plans. All requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic auth injection. Use connectors.proxy("segment", "/path") to invoke endpoints via the proxy. Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},sendgrid:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!0,metadata:{verticals:["other"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-sendgrid.svg",stage:"ga",authType:"API_KEY"}},sharepoint:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"SharePoint Online",visibility:"ga",vertical:["file-storage","communication"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-sharepoint.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to SharePoint Online to manage sites, drives, lists, and pages via the Graph API.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the SharePoint Online connector via the proxy pattern. Common useful endpoints include:\n• GET /sites (list sites)\n• GET /drives or GET /drive (retrieve document libraries or default drive)\n• GET /lists (manage lists)\n• GET or POST /sites/{site-id}/pages (manage SharePoint pages)\nRequests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth2 token injection and refresh. Use: connectors.proxy("sharepoint", "/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""},integrationKeys:{nango:"sharepoint"}}},slack:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Slack",visibility:"ga",vertical:["other"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-slack.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Slack to interact with channels, messages, users, and manage auth.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Slack connector via the proxy pattern. Common useful Slack Web API endpoints include: GET /conversations.list, POST /chat.postMessage, GET /users.list, POST /conversations.inviteShared, and GET /conversations.history. All requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth token injection—just call connectors.proxy("slack", "/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},"slack-agent":{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!0,metadata:{verticals:["communication"],displayName:"Slack Agent",stage:"beta",logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-slack.svg"}},"slack-agent-builder":{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!0,metadata:{verticals:["communication"],displayName:"Slack Agent Builder",stage:"beta",logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-slack.svg",authType:"OAUTH2"}},"slack-deployed-agent":{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Slack Deployed Agent",visibility:"ga",vertical:["other"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-slack.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Slack Deployed Agent to access its API.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Slack Deployed Agent connector via the proxy pattern for authenticated API requests. All requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth token injection and refresh. Prefer using: connectors.proxy("slack-deployed-agent", "/endpoint"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},snowflake:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Snowflake",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["developer-tools"],audience:["enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-snowflake.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Snowflake to execute SQL statements and manage resources via REST API.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Snowflake connector via the proxy pattern. Common useful API endpoints include: POST /api/v2/statements/ to submit SQL, GET /api/v2/statements/{statementHandle} to check status, POST /api/v2/statements/{statementHandle}/cancel to cancel execution. All requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic auth injection—use connectors.proxy("snowflake", "/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},spotify:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Spotify (OAuth)",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["other"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-spotify.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Spotify (OAuth) to access user data and control playback via RESTful API.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'To use the Spotify connector via the proxy pattern, the agent can call common endpoints such as:\n• GET /v1/me/playlists — get current user’s playlists\n• GET /v1/playlists/{playlist_id}/items — get tracks in a playlist\n• GET /v1/me/player — get current playback state\n• PUT /v1/me/player/play — start/resume playback\n• PUT /v1/me/player/pause — pause playback\nRequests are proxied through the SDK with automatic auth injection. Use connectors.proxy("spotify", "/path") for all requests. Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},sproutsocial:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Sprout Social",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["social-media"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-sproutsocial.svg",authType:"API_KEY",description:"Connect to Sprout Social to access and manage social profiles, analytics, posts, and media.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Sprout Social connector via the proxy pattern to interact with key endpoints. Common API calls include: GET /v1/metadata/client, GET /v1/{customerID}/metadata/customer, POST /v1/{customerID}/media/, and GET /v1/{customerID}/metadata/customer/tags. Requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic auth injection—simply use connectors.proxy("sproutsocial", "/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},stripe:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!0,metadata:{verticals:["commerce"],displayName:"Stripe",logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-stripe.svg",stage:"beta",authType:"API_KEY"}},"stripe-agent-sandbox":{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!0,metadata:{verticals:["commerce"],displayName:"Stripe Agent Sandbox",logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-stripe.svg",stage:"beta"}},todoist:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Todoist",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["ticketing"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-todoist.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Todoist to manage tasks, projects, labels, and sections.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Todoist connector via the proxy pattern for authenticated API requests. Common endpoints: GET /api/v1/tasks to list tasks, GET /api/v1/projects to list projects, GET /api/v1/labels to list labels, GET /api/v1/sections?project_id={project_id} to list sections in a project, POST /api/v1/tasks to create a task. All requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic OAuth token injection. Prefer using: connectors.proxy("todoist", "/api/v1/tasks"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{javascript:[{package_name:"@doist/todoist-api-typescript",package_version:"3.0.3"}]}},links:{webUrl:"https://todoist.com",apiDocsUrl:"https://developer.todoist.com/api/v1"},integrationKeys:{nango:"todoist"}}},twilio:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!0,metadata:{verticals:["communication"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-twilio.svg",stage:"ga",authType:"API_KEY"}},workato:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!0,metadata:{verticals:["other"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-workato.svg",stage:"ga",authType:"API_KEY"}},x:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"X",visibility:"ga",vertical:["social-media"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-x.svg",authType:"API_KEY",description:"Connect to X to access public posts, users, spaces, direct messages, lists, and trends.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the X connector via the proxy pattern to interact with common API v2 endpoints: GET /2/tweets/search/stream (filtered stream), POST /2/tweets/search/stream/rules (manage stream rules), GET /2/users/by/username/:username (lookup user information). All requests are proxied through connectors.proxy("x", "/path") with automatic auth injection. Prefer using: connectors.proxy("x", "/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},youtube:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"YouTube",visibility:"ga",vertical:["communication"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-youtube.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to YouTube to interact with videos, channels, playlists, and more.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the YouTube connector via the proxy pattern. Proxy through common endpoints like GET /videos, GET /search, POST /playlists, PUT /subscriptions, DELETE /playlistItems. Remember that requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic auth injection. Prefer using: connectors.proxy("youtube", "/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""},integrationKeys:{nango:"youtube"}}},zendesk:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Zendesk",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["ticketing"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-zendesk.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Zendesk to create, update, list tickets and users via Support API.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use this connector to interact with Zendesk Support APIs via proxies. Common endpoints include: POST /api/v2/tickets to create a ticket; PUT /api/v2/tickets/update_many to update multiple tickets; GET /api/v2/users to list users; POST /api/v2/oauth/tokens to generate OAuth access tokens; GET /api/v2/tickets to list tickets. Requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic auth injection — use connectors.proxy("zendesk", "/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""}}},zoom:{hasClient:!1,hasServer:!1,metadata:{displayName:"Zoom",visibility:"alpha",vertical:["streaming"],audience:["paid","enterprise"],logoUrl:"/_assets/logo-zoom.svg",authType:"OAUTH2",description:"Connect to Zoom to manage users, meetings, recordings, and more.",blueprint:{agentInstructions:'Use the Zoom OAuth2 connector via the proxy pattern to interact with Zoom resources. Common useful endpoints include: GET /users (list users), GET /users/{userId}/meetings (list user’s meetings), POST /users/{userId}/meetings (create meeting), GET /meetings/{meetingId}/recordings (list recordings), DELETE /webhooks/{webhookId} (delete a webhook). Remember: requests are proxied through the SDK with automatic auth injection — use connectors.proxy("zoom", "/path"). Note: the proxy returns a raw response object, not parsed JSON — call .json() to parse the response body.',packages:{}},links:{webUrl:"",apiDocsUrl:""},integrationKeys:{nango:"zoom"}}}},ou=on.enum(Object.keys(oc)).openapi({ref:"core.connector.name"});function ol(e){return ou.safePars